# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository and on checkout, regardless of
# a contributor's core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows clone with
# autocrlf=true rewrites files to CRLF, producing whole-file diffs (and, for *.sh,
# bash failures: "$'\r': command not found"). text=auto lets git auto-detect and
# leave binary files untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt-and-suspenders for files that MUST stay LF to run in the Linux container.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# ...and the mirror image: Windows-only entry points MUST be checked out with CRLF.
# cmd.exe is only reliably correct on CRLF batch files -- an LF-only .cmd works for trivial
# cases but misbehaves around labels, goto, and multi-line blocks, which is a miserable thing
# to debug remotely. The repo still STORES them as LF; only the working copy is CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
